#!/usr/bin/env python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
"""
h713-install -- turn an HY310/H713 projector over to Linux, from a PC.

Runs on Linux and Windows, with Python 3.9+ and without further packages.
Specification: doku/110-plan-installationsweg.md.

The whole procedure in four steps:

  1. Put the device into FEL mode: hold the reset button, plug the power in.
     (No opening the case, no pad, no soldering.)
  2. Start this tool. It loads U-Boot volatile over USB -- NOT one byte is
     written onto the eMMC while doing so -- and lets it expose the eMMC as a
     USB drive.
  3. It takes a dump (size of your choice), fetches the device's own parts out
     of it and writes the new image.
  4. Power off and on again. Done.

The only way out of the drive exposure is a power cycle -- that is no defect
but the end of the road: afterwards the new system starts anyway.

With --ssh-key FILE your own public SSH key goes into the image, as
/root/.ssh/authorized_keys (mode 0600, root's). Without it there is no ssh
access, only the serial console -- the image deliberately carries no key
(doku/107 §3).
"""

# Stage 3 of doku/121: one tool with subcommands, English throughout, the files found by
# themselves. The steps are the old main()/_arbeiten() of hy310-install.py, split by
# subcommand -- same steps, same order, same exit codes; the command line and the language
# are what changed. The German switches live on as hidden aliases for one release.

